You are a VERIFIER for one tech-debt finding in `/Users/david/projects/HiloAviation/hilo-figma-atos`. Confirm it against the ACTUAL code (open the referenced files with Read) — do not trust the finder.
Finding: {"title":"buildStructurePrompt has no division-by-zero guard on lesson-duration inputs","severity":"LOW","area":"Input validation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-curriculum-generator.ts"],"detail":"Lines 81-90: `Math.ceil((answers.totalFlightHours * 60) / answers.flightLessonDurationMin)` and the ground/sim equivalents divide directly by user-supplied `flightLessonDurationMin` / `groundLessonDurationMin` with no check for zero or negative values. If a client sends `0`, the result is `Infinity` or `NaN`, which gets embedded directly into the prompt text sent to Claude (e.g. 'Flight lessons: Infinity × 0 min').","impact":"Malformed request produces a nonsensical prompt sent to the paid AI API, wasting a call and likely getting a garbage/error structure response rather than a clean validation rejection.","recommendation":"Validate `flightLessonDurationMin`, `groundLessonDurationMin`, `simLessonDurationMin` are positive integers before calling buildStructurePrompt; return 400 otherwise.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

